# Artifact system

Tracked work lives in `.cursor/artifacts.db` (SQLite, WAL mode). The `artifact` CLI manages records.

## When the user references a task or item to work on

1. Query active artifacts:
   ```bash
   sqlite3 .cursor/artifacts.db "SELECT id, title, status, next, domain FROM artifacts WHERE status != 'done' ORDER BY updated DESC LIMIT 20"
   ```
2. Match their request to an artifact by title/domain
3. Read full context: `sqlite3 .cursor/artifacts.db "SELECT * FROM artifacts WHERE id='<id>'"`

## After completing work on a tracked artifact

Update its status:
```bash
artifact emit --kind <kind> --domain <domain> --id <local-id> \
  --title "..." --status <done|active|waiting|needs-me|stale> \
  --last-action "<what you just did>" --next "<what's needed next>"
```

## Status values

`done` | `active` | `waiting` | `needs-me` | `stale`

## Other commands

- `artifact suggest --text "..." --source-skill <skill>` — log system improvement ideas
- `artifact link --from <id> --to <id> --rel <feeds-into|depends-on|tracks|dupes>` — connect artifacts
- `artifact init-db` — create/update schema

## Convention

- Re-emitting the same artifact ID with a new `--status` is how status changes
- Artifact ID format: `<kind>/<domain>/<local-id>`
- Kind schemas: `smith-xyz/agent-skills/shared/schemas/kinds/*.yaml`
